Z||000000||CanadianGT||04-23-2001||06:10 PM||||Well I was on the way to my bank to get money to pay off the last bit of the rebuild I just got done on my 86GT, and I pulled out of the parking lot right behind a Fiero.  I think it was probably an 86 with the v6, but it was not a GT.  When the light turned green I heared the beautiful sound oh his v6, and he was shifting really hard.  I wanted to get his attention to tell him about this fourm and talk about his car, but he was to hard to keep up with as he was swerving in and out of traffic.  "DARN IT", I thought.  So i turned left at the next light,  and there was an another FIERO in front of me!!  A blue 87.  Didn't have to get his attention though, as I ran into him just recently and already told him about the forum!!  I feel Like a stalker! Even though Im new on the forum I am already recruiting!<BR>Oh well. Us Fiero Guys got to stick together!<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||04-24-2001||06:37 PM||||I confess, I tend to be a "Fiero stalker" sometimes, too!  Hopefully I haven't scared anybody off -!  Just have to be reasonably polite about it, I guess.<P>The ideal thing, is where I get to stop and talk with the driver.  If I'm <B>really</B> lucky, they'll start telling me how much trouble they're having with the car, or how they're outgrowing it, etc.  I can always use another one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||10
